{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/unital_groebner_decomposition.lean#L60-L86","doc":"**Free-module decomposition — `Õ(G)`-component.**\n\nFor a Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys` whose rules have unit leading\ncoefficients, every element `f` reduces to a normal form (the\n`Õ(G)`-summand of `f` in `A = I ⊕ Õ(G)`).\n\nThe flatness conjunct it used to carry was false as stated and is\nremoved (2026-11-15); see the module docstring. `hgs` is kept so the\nsignature still names the GS-basis hypothesis of the manuscript\ntheorem, though this half does not use it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:unital-groebner-decomposition","label":"thm:unital-groebner-decomposition","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}